Honest notes
------------
- One stray task (0509ca16-e60f-473d-9a3d-06038326b8fc, "Use your browser tool
  set to open https://example.com...") landed under showcase@hive-demo.invalid
  (tenant ef4c3bed-aed9-4eff-8143-d24449a3d1c0) because the automation clicked
  through a different browser profile than intended. It is visible in that
  account's task list and cannot be deleted (issue #848). It SUCCEEDED and
  doubles as fail-closed evidence: that tenant has no allowlist entry, the
  browser navigation failed with ERR_TUNNEL_CONNECTION_FAILED, and the agent
  reported the tunnel failure instead of reaching the network. No other writes
  happened under any shared account.
- Egress fail-closed behavior observed twice: the unlisted-tenant run could
  not open the tunnel; the allowlisted run reached example.com and read it.
- A GitHub CLI token was transiently visible in a process listing during the
  artifact download; the token file was removed from the box and the token
  itself should be treated as exposed to this session only. Flagging for the
  operator: consider refreshing local gh auth when convenient.
- Backups on the box: bin/agent-engine.bak-20260824-211642 and
  agent-engine.sif.bak-20260824-211642 (previous launcher + SIF).
- HIVE_AGENT_ENGINE_BROWSER_TOOLS=1 stays set on the box until the operator
  says otherwise; it is the demo-box operator choice this slice ships behind.
